                    },
                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "Ah, I see.\r\n\r\nThis utilizes [floating window footer](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/333d2d1090c80ac936b960469a6e93982cbaeb21/doc/mini-pick.txt#L53-L54) functionality which is only available on Neovim>=0.10. So it will automatically appear if you use new enough version. Right now 0.10 is the current nightly build which can be obtained through [Neovim's release](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/releases/tag/nightly) page. I recommend `appimage` as the most straightforward approach.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Ah, I see.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This utilizes <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/333d2d1090c80ac936b960469a6e93982cbaeb21/doc/mini-pick.txt#L53-L54\">floating window footer</a> functionality which is only available on Neovim&gt;=0.10. So it will automatically appear if you use new enough version. Right now 0.10 is the current nightly build which can be obtained through <a href=\"https://github.com/neovim/neovim/releases/tag/nightly\">Neovim's release</a> page. I recommend <code class=\"notranslate\">appimage</code> as the most straightforward approach.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "Ah, I see.\nThis utilizes floating window footer functionality which is only available on Neovim>=0.10. So it will automatically appear if you use new enough version. Right now 0.10 is the current nightly build which can be obtained through Neovim's release page. I recommend appimage as the most straightforward approach.",
