        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61948252?u=4fe2afd5d8de7d3ee7b41a2ec5e9987bbcbf2f23&v=4",
                "login": "lostl1ght",
                "resourcePath": "/lostl1ght",
                "url": "https://github.com/lostl1ght"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "I've found that changing and restoring the cursor shape with mini.pick's events works great.\r\nYour terminal or GUI must support styling the cursor `:h 'guicursor'`.\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/61948252/d779563a-ea43-490a-807e-f5b462829c19)\r\n\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal guicursor = vim.opt.guicursor:get()\r\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('User', {\r\n  pattern = 'MiniPickStart',\r\n  callback = function() vim.opt.guicursor = { 'n:hor1' } end,\r\n})\r\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('User', {\r\n  pattern = 'MiniPickStop',\r\n  callback = function() vim.opt.guicursor = guicursor end,\r\n})\r\n```",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">I've found that changing and restoring the cursor shape with mini.pick's events works great.<br>\nYour terminal or GUI must support styling the cursor <code class=\"notranslate\">:h 'guicursor'</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/61948252/346728262-d779563a-ea43-490a-807e-f5b462829c19.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..e2t4ajgp38aQNyiCYYDbCSrF-dQcLOAae7AgwcIbcDI\"><img src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/61948252/346728262-d779563a-ea43-490a-807e-f5b462829c19.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..e2t4ajgp38aQNyiCYYDbCSrF-dQcLOAae7AgwcIbcDI\" alt=\"image\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"></a></p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"local guicursor = vim.opt.guicursor:get()\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('User', {\n  pattern = 'MiniPickStart',\n  callback = function() vim.opt.guicursor = { 'n:hor1' } end,\n})\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('User', {\n  pattern = 'MiniPickStop',\n  callback = function() vim.opt.guicursor = guicursor end,\n})\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">guicursor</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">opt</span>.<span class=\"pl-en\">guicursor</span>:<span class=\"pl-c1\">get</span>()\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">api</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">nvim_create_autocmd</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>User<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, {\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">pattern</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>MiniPickStart<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>,\n  <span class=\"pl-en\">callback</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>() <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">opt</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">guicursor</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>n:hor1<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span>} <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>,\n})\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">api</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">nvim_create_autocmd</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>User<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, {\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">pattern</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>MiniPickStop<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>,\n  <span class=\"pl-en\">callback</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>() <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">opt</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">guicursor</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">guicursor</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>,\n})</pre></div>",
            "bodyText": "I've found that changing and restoring the cursor shape with mini.pick's events works great.\nYour terminal or GUI must support styling the cursor :h 'guicursor'.\n\nlocal guicursor = vim.opt.guicursor:get()\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('User', {\n  pattern = 'MiniPickStart',\n  callback = function() vim.opt.guicursor = { 'n:hor1' } end,\n})\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('User', {\n  pattern = 'MiniPickStop',\n  callback = function() vim.opt.guicursor = guicursor end,\n})",
